2.9 逻辑回归的梯度下降（Logistic Regression Gradient Descent）
> logistic regression recap:
z=w^T.x+b, y-hat=a=σ(z)=1/(1+e^-z) =(1+e^-z)^-1
L(a, y)=-(ylog(y-hat) +(1-y)log(1-y-hat))=-[(ylog(a)+(1-y)log(1-a))]
#if we have two features x1, x2, so 
z=w1x1+w2x2+b --> y-hat=a=σ(z) --> L(a, y) 
#how to compute backwards?
> logistic regression derivatives: 
z=w1x1+w2x2+b --> y-hat=a=σ(z) --> L(a, y) 
da=dL(a,y)/da=dL/da*(da/dz)=(-y/a + (-1)*(1-y)/(1-a)*(-1)) *(da/dz)=-y/a+(1-y)/(1-a) 
dz=dL/dz=dL(a,y)/dz=dL/da*(da/dz)
da/dz=(-1)*(1+e^-z)^-2*((-1)*e^-z)=e^-z/(1+e^-z)^2=a(1-a) #sigmoid function derivative 
da=dL(a,y)/da=(-y/a+(1-y)/(1-a))*a(1-a)=a-y 
dL/dw1=x1.dL/dz=dw1, dw2=x2.dL/dz=dw2, db=dL/dz

2.10 梯度下降的例子(Gradient Descent on m Examples)
> logistic regression on m examples: 
J(w,b)=1/m*∑(i=1 to m)L(a^(i),y^(i)) 
a^(i)0y-hat^(i)=G(z^(i))=G(w^T.x^(i)+b),  dw1^(i), dw2^(i), db^(i) #one single training example 
dJ(w,b)/dw1=1/m*∑(i=1 to m)dL(a^(i),y^(i))/dw1,dL(a^(i),y^(i))/dw1=dw1^(i)
let us say:
J=0, dw1=0, dw2=0, db=0 #初始化
for i=1 to m 
z^(i)= w^T.x^(i)+b  #z^(i）=w1x1^(i)+w2x2^(i)+b 
a^(i)=G(z^(i)) #a^(i)=sigma(z^(i))=1/(1+e^-z^(i)) 
J+=-(y^(i)log(a^(i))+(1-y^(i))log(1-a^(i)))
dz^(i)+=a^(i)-y^(i) #L=-[ylog(a)+(1-y)log(1-a)], dL/dz=dL/da*da/dz=(-y/a+(1-y)/(1-a))*a(1-a)=a^(i)-y^(i) 
dw1^(i)+=x1^(i)*dz^(i), dw2^(i)+=x2^(i)*dz^(i), db^(i)+=dz^(i)
w1=w1-α*dw1, w2=w2-α*dw2, b=b-α*db #update parameters
#here are two weakness here: for loop over all the features over all training examples. so vectorization is needed 

